  "description": {
    "de": "The National Park Thayatal administration ordered a scientific study about the soils of the Austrian\npart of this cross-border protected area in Summer 2024. The fieldwork for the soil survey was\nconducted between August and October 2024 obtaining 15 soil profile descriptions and two\nrepresentative soil cores for demonstration purposes. The soil classification system has been applied\nbased on a substrate type map on the basis of the geological maps of Austria, sheet 8 Geras and 9\nRetz. For all important substrate type combinations the possible soil types in the investigated area\nhave been defined and representatively sampled. The soil profiles together with soil punctures build\nthe data basis for the calibration of the soil type model being translated into a soil type map using relief\nform and slope raster by GIS methods. The resulting cartographic entities in addition to the substrate\ntype provide information about the relevant soils and soil depths as well as ecological site information\nlike water holding capacity and nutrient supply.\n"
  },
